Everything is working now.

**Diagnosis:** The `pip` Python package was missing from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/` — only the `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` metadata directory remained. The actual `pip/` package directory had been deleted or corrupted, so the `pip3` script (which lives in `/usr/local/bin/`) couldn't import the `pip` module.

**Fix:** Removed the orphaned `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` directory and re-ran `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade`, which reinstalled the full pip package from the bundled wheel. Both `pip3` and `python3 -m pip` are now functional.

